Shall we check `Schema.UniqueKeys` as well? AFAICS, the result of common aggregations on columns would not be impacted by the `null` values in the column. e.g,

```sql
create table t(a int, unique key(a));
explain select count(distinct) a from t;
```

@winoros can you think of any aggregation case that would break this assumption?
